`immediateDelete` doesn't delete the database record, only cancels the SendGrid job

When `immediateDelete=true`, the function returns early after canceling the SendGrid job but never deletes the `WorkflowReminder` from the database. This leaves orphaned records that are marked as cancelled but never cleaned up.

```suggestion
    if (immediateDelete) {
      await client.request({
        url: "/v3/user/scheduled_sends",
        method: "POST",
        body: {
          batch_id: referenceId,
          status: "cancel",
        },
      });

      await prisma.workflowReminder.delete({
        where: {
          id: reminderId,
        },
      });
      return;
    }
```

The `OR` logic deletes reminders that satisfy EITHER condition, which means ALL workflow reminders (SMS and non-SMS) with `retryCount > 1` are deleted regardless of their `scheduledDate` or `method`. This will delete valid reminders from other workflow types.

The `OR` should be `AND`, and the `retryCount` check should be inside the first condition:

```suggestion
      OR: [
        {
          method: WorkflowMethods.SMS,
          scheduledDate: {
            lte: dayjs().toISOString(),
          },
          retryCount: {
            gt: 1,
          },
        },
      ],
```

